# Weapons Manufacturing triggers only for a nontoken artifact its controller controls. Turn 1 Bot1 casts it with two Moxen.
# Turn 2 Bot2 casts a Lotus Petal: an artifact under the opponent's control, no Munitions. Turn 3 Bot1 plays a Mountain (not
# an artifact), then sacrifices Mox Ruby to Deadly Dispute for a Treasure token (an artifact token, not nontoken): still no
# Munitions, and the stack is empty throughout. The positive control, a nontoken artifact of Bot1's making one, is
# weapons-manufacturing-makes-munitions-that-deal-two-damage-when-sacrificed.

